# Kind-classification mini-gold seed (issue #1695, Task 2 / D0-3).
#
# THIS IS THE SCHEMA + PIPELINE FIXTURE — NOT the full D0-3 gold set.
# The real D0-3 gold (>=2000 bits/arm, owner+adjudicator labels, 10%
# agreement check, calibrate/holdout split) is authored at RUN level
# (production S1 capture post-#1468; fallback dev/product-strategy sessions
# + trigger-bearing synthetic transcripts) per the plan's Step 2 — this
# committed seed pins the bit-level eval schema, the metadata checks in
# tests/test_kind_eval_set.py, and gives the D0-2 probe a stable in-domain
# instrument.
#
# Bit schema (one JSON object per line):
#   id           str  — stable content-derived id
#   content      str  — the extracted bit (entity name / event content /
#                       point content) the classifier must kind
#   type         str  — "entity" | "event" | "point"
#   gold_kind    str  — the ABSOLUTE gold label (namespaced, from the master
#                       list vocabulary; NEVER "unclassified")
#   split        str  — "calibrate" | "holdout"
#   near_miss_of [str] — kinds this bit is designed to confound (optional)
#   provenance   dict — {source, author, date, note} (owner + adjudicator
#                       labeling with conflict rule, 10% agreement check
#                       on the full set)
#
# Sentinel rule: "unclassified" is a SEPARATE bounded class in the eval
# (sentinel rate <= 5% gate) — gold bits never carry it.

